00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.240
for each ingredient,

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.620
to then construct the
ultimate reheat method.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.280
We're going to go oven.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.970
350 sounds like a pretty
decent starting point.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:30.160
I think I'm going to wrap
the whole thing in foil

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.152
and toss some fries on the side.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:34.770
(foil crinkling)

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.680
- I want to make sure they all have room.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:38.513
Toss that in.

00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:40.080
It's been about 5 minutes.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.167
Ooh, sizzling a little bit.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:43.430
I'm going to give that a little flip.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:44.540
Toss around.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.560
AlRight. It's been about 10 minutes.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.280
I think it's time to eat our oven test.

00:02:48.280 --> 00:02:49.560
Ooh, hot, hot, hot.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:50.500
Immediate thoughts.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.453
I'm liking the way the fries look.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.130
The fries are serious.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.810
If these were in the oven for any longer,

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.810
